[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Constraint reporting and energy qualification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-CONSTRAINT-OUTPUT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Report constitutive constraints independently of conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
DC audit reports shall include named constraints for inductors, CCVS and
behavioral voltage sources. A manufactured state satisfying KCL and total power
but violating the device voltage equation shall fail the corresponding named
constraint. Absence of a constraint is not a passing constraint.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: audit_output_contracts dc_inductor_constraint_is_present_and_rejects_a_conservation_consistent_voltage,
ccvs_constraint_uses_the_signed_nonzero_sensing_current and
behavioral_voltage_constraint_and_relative_bound_use_differential_magnitudes.
Known source/load states are specified analytically without a solver or Jacobian.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-VOLTAGE-BOUND-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Voltage-equation tolerance uses absolute physical magnitudes
STATEMENT: >>>
The effective voltage-constraint tolerance shall equal its configured absolute
voltage bound plus relative times the sum of absolute actual and expected
voltages. Signed cancellation or multiplication of those magnitudes shall not
replace that sum. Behavioral control shall use V(cp)-V(cn), including nonzero
negative control terminals and common control translations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: behavioral_voltage_constraint_and_relative_bound_use_differential_magnitudes.
The manufactured correct state has actual=expected=2*control, giving an
independent bound absolute+relative*2*abs(expected). Three drives and offsets.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-MOS-ENERGY-QUAL-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Distinguish unavailable charged-MOS energy from checked memoryless balance
STATEMENT: >>>
Until its nonlinear charge energy audit is qualified, a charged intrinsic MOS1
step shall report be_energy_balance as NotChecked with unavailable numeric
metrics and an explanatory reason. A memoryless MOS1 stationary step with a
known balanced source/conduction state shall retain its measured passing energy
check. Adding or removing oxide charge shall not fabricate or suppress evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: mos_charge_energy_qualification_is_not_a_fabricated_numeric_pass.
Zero oxide and 3 nF oxide cases use the independently known 75 microamp triode
current and two non-unit timesteps. This does not qualify nonlinear stored energy.
Only arithmetic discarded behind an unchanged NotChecked result may be reviewed
as currently unobservable; preserve each raw outcome and reassess if metrics,
logging, qualification or floating execution semantics change. Retain guards.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-POWER-BOUND-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Include shunt dissipation in absolute power scaling
STATEMENT: >>>
The measured power-balance tolerance shall include the absolute magnitudes of
source, load and explicit Gmin shunt powers. Cancellation of signed powers shall
not remove those terms from the relative tolerance scale.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: nonunit_gmin_power_bound_counts_source_load_and_shunt_magnitudes.
A 2 V source, 2 ohm load and shunt G have signed powers -(2+4G), 2 and 4G W,
and absolute sum 4+8G W. Three non-unit shunts distinguish scale from residual.
<<<
